{{begin-newsitem |time=2026-10-26T21:57:25Z |title=Namebreaking progress: 70 more names found |author=Ojan |resources=namebreak-small.png |categories=StarCraft I, WarCraft II, modding, Namebreaking |summary=Two weeks after the start, eight people have joined the hunt for the last unknown MPQ filenames, and around 70 more names have been found. The client has also been improved with dictionary search and meet-in-the-middle search}}

Two weeks ago, I [wrote](../archive/october_2026.html#newsitem_2026-10-10T21:46:55Z) about {{highlight |text=namebreak-bombe}}, the tool for cracking the last unknown filenames in Blizzard's MPQ archives on GPUs. A lot has happened since then! At the time it was just me and {{highlight |text=Heinermann}} running it; now people have contributed to the [coordinated search](https://namebreak-coordinator.fly.dev/), and together we have hashed more than 8 quintillion ({{math |eq=8 \cdot 10^18}}) candidate names. A big thanks to everyone who has joined, in particular {{highlight |text=Heinermann}}, {{highlight |text=lucifirius}}, {{highlight |text=Johnny C}}, {{highlight |text=Jesse}} and {{highlight |text=mika}} (and myself!), who have all found names.

{{img |file=namebreak-small.png |title=namebreak-bombe}}


